      "re-running at another volatility target or cost convention to rescue the economics",
      "any nonlinear or ML formulation",
      "reading any protected span, or extending the request past the frozen end date"
    ],
    "publication_lag": {
      "cpi": "the index for month M is used only from the end of month M+2",
      "fx": "the reference rate of day d informs a decision at the close of day d at the earliest, never earlier",
      "quarterly_countries": "Australia and New Zealand publish quarterly; the quarter's value is carried forward under the same lag and the step is not smoothed",
      "vintages": "only revised history is available for most of these series, so the run uses revised data and the bias is disclosed rather than modelled: a revision that arrived after the decision cannot have been known, and this design cannot see that. Any positive result carries that caveat explicitly"
    },
    "question": "does an ex-ante measure of real exchange rate valuation — a currency's nominal value against the basket, adjusted for relative price levels, compared with its own history — predict G10 FX excess returns over the following months, beyond the nominal mean reversion that needs no price levels at all?",
    "robustness_anchor": "one alternative anchor is declared in advance — the expanding median instead of the mean — and reported as a robustness check, never as a selection. If the sign of the result changes between the two, the design is too anchor-dependent and stops",
    "screen": {
      "candidate": "every shared condition holds and C's net Sharpe is at least 0.3",
      "kind": "development screen, symmetric and exhaustive; seen data decides nothing",
      "marginal_candidate": "every shared condition holds and C's net Sharpe is in [0.25, 0.3) with turnover at or below half the bound. The ruling allows this tier for a slow, stable source; it is a tier for returning to Human, never for advancing, and a diversification argument alone may not reach it while the programme has no positive core",
      "no_automatic_progress_to_fresh": true,
      "shared_conditions": [
        "book A gross Sharpe > 0",
        "the primary test C has positive gross and net",
        "C carries a positive net increment over the nominal control B",
        "the valuation ordering is economically sensible: mean forward excess return falls monotonically from the cheap tercile to the dear one",
        "a majority of the temporal blocks are positive",
        "no single currency carries more than half of the gross, and the sign survives dropping any one of the eight",
        "the result is not one episode: removing the best twelve-month window leaves the sign",
        "turnover at or below 12 round trips a year per unit gross",
        "net Sharpe stays positive at 2x and 3x cost",
        "the sign is unchanged under the declared robustness anchor",
        "5% annual net is reachable at a target volatility whose gap stress, measured on this universe, does not force a loss-cut, and whose required volatility is at most 15%"
      ],
      "status_candidate": "REAL_EXCHANGE_RATE_VALUATION_DEVELOPMENT_CANDIDATE",
      "status_data": "REAL_EXCHANGE_RATE_VALUATION_DATA_NOT_DECISION_GRADE",
      "status_marginal": "REAL_EXCHANGE_RATE_VALUATION_MARGINAL_DEVELOPMENT_CANDIDATE",
      "status_stop": "REAL_EXCHANGE_RATE_VALUATION_NOT_SUPPORTED_IN_DEVELOPMENT",
      "stop": "every other outcome, including any failure of a shared condition at any Sharpe"
    },
    "stage": "Stage 1: one unfitted rule, no fitted coefficient, no model, no ML, no search",
    "track": "T-V — real exchange rate valuation",
    "valuation_formula": {
      "anchor": "a_c = the expanding-window mean of q_c using only months already observed, with at least 60 months required before the currency may take a position",
      "deviation": "d_c = q_c - a_c, positive meaning overvalued",
      "no_full_sample_anchor": "the anchor never uses a month the decision could not have seen; a full-sample mean applied backwards is prohibited",
      "nominal_value": "n_c = log of the euro value of one unit of c, cross-sectionally demeaned",
      "real_value": "q_c = n_c + pi_c — a currency whose nominal value has held while its prices rose is dear in real terms",
      "relative_price_level": "pi_c = log CPI_c, cross-sectionally demeaned, at the lagged availability",
      "sign_frozen": true,
